# Line endings
# -----------
# The repository currently holds both LF and CRLF text files (17 files are stored with CRLF,
# see `git ls-files --eol`). A global `* text=auto` would make git report those files as
# modified and convert them on the next commit that touches them. To avoid surprise diffs while
# work is in progress, this file does NOT normalise text files yet; it only marks binary types
# and generated files. Recommended later, in one separate commit when nobody else has open
# changes (see docs/18_veroeffentlichung.md):
#
#     * text=auto
#     *.ps1 text eol=crlf
#     *.sh  text eol=lf
#     # then: git add --renormalize .  &&  git commit -m "Zeilenenden vereinheitlichen"

# Binary files: never diff or merge as text, never convert line endings.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.bin   binary
*.elf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.pdf   binary
*.der   binary
*.cer   binary

# Generated files: collapsed in GitHub diffs, not counted in the language statistics.
firmware/printdrive/main/anim_data.inc        linguist-generated
firmware/components/pd_crypt/xts_vectors.h    linguist-generated
firmware/*/dependencies.lock                  linguist-generated
